","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIMPLE WEAPON\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIZE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DAMAGE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["STUN"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/STUN"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["WEIGHT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["TYPE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["AVAILABILITY\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Wan-Shen"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wan-Shen","referenceId":"reference:a5bef67f37df2da3"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Large\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1,000\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2d6/2d6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["NO\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2 kg\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Slashing and Bludgeoning\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Rare"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rare"},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["1: Can be ",{"tag":"a","children":["Thrown"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Thrown"}]}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["2: Is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reach"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reach"}," weapon"]}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Advanced Lightsaber Construction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Advanced_Lightsaber_Construction"}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["For some Jedi and Sith, a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," is not just a weapon; it is a personalized emblem of one's life and philosophy. Similarly, some players may wish to customize their Jedi hero's Lightsaber to reflect the character's philosophy and fighting style, beyond the basic Lightsaber Construction rules found above. This following section includes a wealth of new options for players and Gamemasters looking to customize their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," to better fit the characters who wield them. The Advanced Lightsaber Construction process begins when a hero reaches 7th level.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ol","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["First, the player or Gamemaster must decide what kind to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," to build. The standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," is the most common ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," in the galaxy, and it is not only the easiest to build but also requires no special training to use effectively in combat (besides the standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Proficiency (Lightsabers)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Proficiency_(Lightsabers)"}," Feat)."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["Once a particular kind of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," has been selected, the next step is to choose a Lightsaber Crystal. Any character can build a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," from an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Adegan Crystal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Adegan_Crystal"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ilum Crystal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ilum_Crystal","referenceId":"reference:d330f9b088faed5d"},", or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Synthetic Crystal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Synthetic_Crystal"},"; the default assumption is that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," (and other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},"-wielding ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Traditions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Traditions","referenceId":"reference:da4e2621bc8ff060"},") have ample access to these Lightsaber Crystals and need perform no special quest to obtain one. However, if you wish to use a Lightsaber Crystal of another kind, the character may need to undergo a special adventure to obtain the Lightsaber Crystal."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["Once the desired Lightsaber Crystal has been chosen and obtained, the next step is to choose any special Lightsaber Accessories or Lightsaber Modifications to be made. With that in mind, the Advanced Lightsaber Construction can begin."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["Special Lightsaber Crystals and Lightsaber Accessories can modify the DC to construct the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},". When Advanced Lightsaber Construction begins, using the standard rules above, applying these modifiers to the standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," check DC before the check is made (the base DC is determined by the type of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," being constructed, per the table blow)."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["Once the Lightsaber is constructed, you may spend a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Point"}," to attune it (a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"},"). From that point on, the creator of this Self-Built Lightsaber gains the benefit of the used Lightsaber Crystal."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Ranged Weapons"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Though the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," is the only weapon most Jedi need, some other weapons occasionally see use among members of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Order"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["EXOTIC WEAPON\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIZE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DAMAGE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["STUN"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/STUN"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["RATE OF FIRE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["WEIGHT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["TYPE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["AVAILABILITY\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Discblade"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Discblade","referenceId":"reference:851ee9a1235d2f50"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Small\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2,000\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2d8\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["NO\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["S\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1.25 kg\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Slashing\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Rare"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rare"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["GRENADE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIZE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DAMAGE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["STUN"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/STUN"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["RATE OF FIRE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["WEIGHT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["TYPE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["AVAILABILITY\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Flash Canister"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flash_Canister","referenceId":"reference:4c1d004318e4524b"},{"tag":"sup","children":["1"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Tiny\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["100\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Special\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["NO\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["S\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0.5 kg\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Energy\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Restricted"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Restricted"},"\n"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["1: Is an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Area Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Area_Attack"}," weapon"]}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Armor"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Though ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," don't typically wear armor, in some dire cases it becomes necessary. Of course, ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," and other Dark Side Force-users are not so reluctant, and many famous Sith Lords are practically defined by their armor.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["ARMOR\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["REFLEX"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/REFLEX"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["FORTITUDE"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/FORTITUDE"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MAX DEX BONUS\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["WEIGHT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["AVAILABILITY\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["LIGHT ARMOR (-2)\n"],"colspan":7}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Light Dark Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Light_Dark_Armor","referenceId":"reference:39f9541a0d542dc0"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["10,000\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+4\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+3\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+3\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["10 kg\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Rare"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rare"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Light Jedi Battle Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Light_Jedi_Battle_Armor","referenceId":"reference:5ea985bf36add244"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["4,000\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+3\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+3\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+4\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["6 kg\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Rare"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rare"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Blinding Helmet"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blinding_Helmet","referenceId":"reference:3790989953a9fbb6"},{"tag":"sup","children":["1"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["200\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+0\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+0\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2 kg\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Rare"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rare"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["MEDIUM ARMOR (-5)\n"],"colspan":7}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Armor","referenceId":"reference:bc9b02500e8a7ac1"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["15,000\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+7\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+4\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["16 kg\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Rare"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rare"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Battle Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Battle_Armor","referenceId":"reference:710432a110a197cb"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["6,000\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+3\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["12 kg\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Rare"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rare"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["HEAVY ARMOR (-10)\n"],"colspan":7}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Dark Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Dark_Armor","referenceId":"reference:4ebe001d2c85d006"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["25,000\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+8\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["20 kg\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Rare"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rare"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Orbalisk Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Orbalisk_Armor","referenceId":"reference:b5639f2be0894ffd"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["26 kg\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Rare"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rare"},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["1: Can be worn in tandem with other clothing or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor"},"."]}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Message from the Faculty: Jedi in Armor"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["By and large, Jedi Knights do not wear armor. ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", or the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},", usually provides enough of a defense against incoming attacks. However, from time to time there has been a need for Jedi to wear armor. Particularly in times when ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," are engaged in all-out-war, some Jedi Knights and Jedi Masters don suits of armor not only for the protection it provides but also as a show of solidarity with the troops under their command. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Obi-Wan Kenobi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Obi-Wan_Kenobi","referenceId":"reference:6e84377ee76928db"}," wears a modified suit of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Trooper Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Trooper_Armor"}," during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," as he leads troops into battle as a sign that he is not above them, but one of them."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Most Jedi who choose to wear armor wear the lightweight and durable ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Battle Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Battle_Armor","referenceId":"reference:710432a110a197cb"},". However, in some cases a Jedi might need to don special armor in order to lead troops or (in situations where they lead ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," squadrons) simply to survive in the cockpit of a spacecraft. As an optional rule, Gamemasters can allow ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," (And other heroic characters) to wear any suit of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Light Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Light_Armor","referenceId":"reference:1b329ddc8a34adfe"}," with no ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor Check Penalty"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor_Check_Penalty"}," even when not possessing the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor Proficiency (Light)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor_Proficiency_(Light)","referenceId":"reference:5c5fd1ac409e0220"}," Feat. However, the hero must also forfeit the armor's bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," in addition to the armor's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},"."]},"\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Other Equipment"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Although ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," have little need for material possessions, there are a few items of importance that they keep at hand for training purposes. The following new pieces of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," are available in most eras in which Jedi are prevalent. During the time of Palpatine's Empire, and during the time of Darth Krayt's reborn Empire, these objects are more scarce, and perhaps even illegal.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MEDICAL GEAR\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["WEIGHT\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["8-2A Medical Bundle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/8-2A_Medical_Bundle","referenceId":"reference:874c99a871ace92b"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["200\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1 kg\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Subelectronic Converter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Subelectronic_Converter","referenceId":"reference:e881c9e3a4511aaa"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["23,000\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SURVIVAL GEAR\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["WEIGHT\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Battle Harness"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Battle_Harness","referenceId":"reference:e9594c6a32da0351"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["5,000\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["90 kg\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["TOOL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["WEIGHT\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Detector"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Detector","referenceId":"reference:425e31f3388d43b9"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2,000\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["9 kg\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Training Aid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Training_Aid","referenceId":"reference:1fc9cd1760ca8b6a"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["25\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1 kg\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Universal Energy Cage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Universal_Energy_Cage","referenceId":"reference:3378de3f3ecc7bb2"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["20,000\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["3 Tons\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Holocrons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Holocrons","referenceId":"reference:78fdd3622bfea307"}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["There are few artifacts in the galaxy that are more highly valued and more unique than Holocrons. Holocrons are, essentially, special computers with built-in holoprojectors that contain vast knowledge of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},". Each Holocron is a small, hand-held device (usually taking the form of some common geometric shape). Holocrons use ancient construction methods to combine powerful crystals with other technological elements to enhance its storage capabilities and durability. Though ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Order"}," does not allow the study of Holocrons by outside technicians, most technological experts agree that the nature of the Holocron indicates that its inner workings are vastly more complex than most modern technologies, and that the components and workings of the Holocron follow few, if any, contemporary theories of how computers and other electronic machinery should work. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In truth, a Holocron is more of an artifact than a technological device. Each Holocron is imbued with at least one \"Gatekeeper\" personality, which serves as the user interface to the library of knowledge stored within. A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Holocron Gatekeeper"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Holocron_Gatekeeper"}," is far more than a simple voice-interface user interface; the Gatekeeper has its own personality and is usually based on an individual ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Master"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Master","referenceId":"reference:5fac760c8a2485ba"}," (or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lord","referenceId":"reference:099f599e53fbfc32"},") who was instrumental in creating the Holocron. Most Holocrons have only a single Gatekeeper, as the Holocron represents the sum total of the knowledge of its creator. Some rare Holocrons have multiple ",{"tag":"a","children":["Holocron Gatekeepers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Holocron_Gatekeepers"},", each one acting as a means of obtaining subsets of knowledge. For example, a Jedi Holocron might have a Weapon Master Gatekeeper to impart knowledge of fighting styles, while also having an Investigator Gatekeeper responsible for all of the Holocron's knowledge of ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Farseeing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Farseeing","referenceId":"reference:efdb098bc15b650e"}]}," techniques.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The depth of a Holocron's knowledge varies, but suffice to say that every Holocron has within it a vast amount of information on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Powers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Powers","referenceId":"reference:85acec94cd1ca5f3"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Techniques"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Techniques"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Secrets"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Secrets"},". Any given Holocron usually contains the sum total of all knowledge of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," gleaned by an individual ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lord","referenceId":"reference:099f599e53fbfc32"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Master"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Master","referenceId":"reference:5fac760c8a2485ba"},", and in many cases it can contain more than that. Many ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Masters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Masters"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic Era"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic_Era"},", as well as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lords"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lords"}," from all ",{"tag":"a","children":["Eras of Play"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Eras_of_Play","referenceId":"reference:8e95f83b34b3926d"},", see the creation of a Holocron as a crucial part of preserving their legacies. Though Sith sometimes linger as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Spirits"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side_Spirits"}," and some Jedi remain can remain as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Spirits"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Spirits"},", a Holocron is a far more permanent representation of their legacies. Though the art of creating a Holocron is among the rarest secrets in the galaxy, the most powerful Sith Lords and Jedi Masters of old create Holocrons to spread their influence and preserve their knowledge for ages.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Sith Holocrons"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Unlike normal Holocrons, a Sith Holocron can have a corrupting influence on its possessor. Sith Holocrons contain forbidden knowledge of great power, and serve only to enhance the reputation of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," for being the quick and easy path. A young student of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," in possession of a Sith Holocron can quickly come into possession of dark knowledge that is forbidden to most Jedi Knights.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A character with a Sith Holocron can be considered part of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," Force Tradition for the purposes of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Apprentice"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Apprentice","referenceId":"reference:580167d0bdd39739"}," Prestige Class. Furthermore, a character that spends at least 1 hour studying under the tutelage of a Sith Holocron can spend a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Point"}," as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"}," to add one ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Power"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Power"}," with the [",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side"}]},"] descriptor to his or her ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Power Suite"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Power_Suite"},". That character can do this for one day; the following day, he or she must study for at least 1 hour with the Sith Holocron before gaining access to this ability again.\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Sith Artifacts"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Several artifacts of great power and significance were created in the time of ancient Sith Lords. Though most Sith of the modern eras tend to eschew the arcane and esoteric knowledge used to create these artifacts, remnants of these dark objects still lie undiscovered in forgotten tombs across the galaxy. Sith Artifacts are considered priceless; thus, they have no costs associated with them.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Amulet"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Amulet","referenceId":"reference:808a67262773c680"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Poison"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Poison","referenceId":"reference:1df10abcb4cabdab"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Talisman"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Talisman","referenceId":"reference:a58248a098943429"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Muur Talisman"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Muur_Talisman","referenceId":"reference:bd015a4f083f9d1e"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Scrolls, Tomes, and Tablets"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Scrolls,_Tomes,_and_Tablets"}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
